./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38023:This attribute is ignored if it not accompanied by an fo:text-align 20.223 attribute.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38027:The fo:text-align-last attribute is usable with the following element: <style:paragraph-properties> 17.6.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38029:The values of the fo:text-align-last attribute are start, center or justify.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:38891:•true: line height is calculated only from the font height as specified by the font size attributes fo:font-size 20.190, style:font-size-asian 20.284 and style:font-size-complex 20.285. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39375:1)Values of attributes fo:border-top 20.183.6, fo:border-bottom 20.183.3, fo:border-left 20.183.4 and fo:border-right 20.183.5 are the same. These values can also be given by the fo:border 20.183.2 attribute. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39383:5)Values of the fo:margin-left 20.207 attribute, which can also be given by the fo:margin, and fo:text-indent 19.246 attributes, that meet one of these conditions: 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39386:2.Values of the fo:margin-left attributes are the same and values of the fo:text-indent attributes are non-negative. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39388:3.Value of the fo:margin-left attribute of one paragraph whose value of the fo:text-indent attribute is non-negative is the same as the sum of values of the fo:margin-left and fo:text-indent attributes of the other paragraph whose value of the fo:text-indent attribute is negative. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39390:4.Both values of the fo:text-indent attributes are negative and the sums of values of the fo:margin-left and fo:text-indent attributes are equal. 
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39408:Specifying a style:justify-single-word attribute without specifying a fo:text-align 20.223 and fo:text-align-last 20.224 attribute has no effect. Unspecified, both fo:text-align and fo:text-align-last have the value start.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39940:20.338 style:rel-column-width
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39942:The style:rel-column-width attribute specifies a relative width of a column with a number value, followed by a ”*” (U+002A, ASTERISK) character. If rc is the relative with of the column, rs the sum of all relative columns widths, and ws the absolute width that is available for these columns the absolute width wc of the column is wc=rcws/rs.
./odf_spec/OpenDocument-v1.4-os-part3-schema.txt:39944:The style:rel-column-width attribute is usable with the following element: <style:table-column-properties> 17.16.
